  "name" : "When running a workflow, how Personas load graph.html-based nodes, from current and parent openloop folders.",
  "summary" : "Yes — graph.html persona context is additive across openloop instances on the path, so a workflow run inside `inner` loads Persona1 node context from both `inner` and `prj`. The runner's `collectContext` walks every directory from curDir up to (excluding) `$HOME`, and for each one containing `.openloop/logs.db` it pulls that instance's Persona1 chain summaries (delivered as separate read-only context files) and unions the MCP endpoints. Caveats: nodes must be active and have a non-empty summary (freshly created or dormant nodes contribute nothing), each instance needs an initialized graph DB, there's no cross-instance chaining or precedence (both contexts always load), and this differs from persona definitions and knowledge folders, which are shadowed by the first match walking up the path.",
  "prompt" : "On `graph.html` I can assign a persona to a node. Openloop also supports personas from parent folders (if they are registed with openloop). Lets say I have path `/some/prj/inner` and `prj` and `inner` folders both have `.openloop`. And for `Persona1` that is defined in `prj` I also created a node in graph.html on `prj` and `inner`. Now when I run a workflow that includes a `Persona1` inside `inner`, will it also load nodes context from `prj`, that I've defined via prj's graph.html?",
  "status" : "success",
